# 05_cv_comparison (5x5 CV comparison, scripts/run_5x5_cv_comparison.py): only the
# small, regeneratable-from-frozen-seeds summary/analysis outputs are tracked --
# summary_table.csv and any notebook-produced statistical results/figures stay
# tracked (NOT ignored), matching 04a_baseline_screen's own summary_table.csv
# treatment. The bulk raw data (300 prediction CSVs, 300 bootstrap score CSVs, ~6.2GB
# of Chemprop checkpoints/logs across 50 chemprop_runs/ subdirs -- a much larger scale
# than 04a's own 10 subdirs, which is why this gets full-directory exclusion instead
# of 04a's per-file-extension approach) is excluded.
logs/*.log
outputs/05_cv_comparison/chemprop_runs/
outputs/05_cv_comparison/predictions/
outputs/05_cv_comparison/scores/

# 06_outlier_check (CYP2D6 outlier check, scripts/cyp2d6_outlier_check.py): same
# treatment as 05_cv_comparison above, for the same reason -- chemprop_runs/ is
# ~12GB of Chemprop checkpoints/logs across 50 subdirs (checked directly). predictions/
# (14MB, 200 files) and scores/ (34MB, 200 files) are individually small but ~48MB
# combined -- also checked directly, not assumed -- so excluded to match 05's own
# predictions/scores precedent; both are fully regeneratable via
# `python scripts/cyp2d6_outlier_check.py --retrain` (deterministic: reuses 05's own
# manifest.csv seeds, the frozen cv_folds.csv partition, and the frozen
# flagged_compounds/*.csv lists). flagged_compounds/*.csv (the frozen threshold audit
# trail) and before_after_comparison.csv (the result table the notebook reports from)
# stay tracked -- both are small and are what the notebook actually reads/writes.
outputs/06_outlier_check/chemprop_runs/
outputs/06_outlier_check/predictions/
outputs/06_outlier_check/scores/

# 07_weighting_tuning (CYP2D6 weighting/tuning, scripts/cyp2d6_weighting_tuning.py):
# same treatment as 05/06 above, for the same reason -- predictions/ (5.8MB, 100
# files), scores/ (17MB, 100 files), and tuning_search/ (200KB, 50 files: one grid
# search per (config, repeat, fold)) are all bulk per-fold raw output, individually
# small but not worth tracking -- checked directly, not assumed. All three are fully
# regeneratable via `python scripts/cyp2d6_weighting_tuning.py --retrain`
# (deterministic: reuses 05's own manifest.csv seeds and the frozen cv_folds.csv
# partition, same as 06). Only the small, notebook-produced summary/analysis outputs
# stay tracked -- step2_summary.csv, the before/after comparison CSVs, figures/ (the
# search-landscape heatmaps are themselves derived-and-aggregated from tuning_search/,
# matching 05's "notebook-produced statistical results/figures" precedent), and
# weighting_check/ (the confirmed per-fold weight distribution, the sanity-check audit
# trail). No chemprop_runs/ -- this step is tabular-only (chemprop_chemeleoninit
# deferred, see the script/notebook intro).
outputs/07_weighting_tuning/predictions/
outputs/07_weighting_tuning/scores/
outputs/07_weighting_tuning/tuning_search/

# 08_ensemble_selection (simple-average ensemble selection, notebook-only -- no
# companion script): same treatment as 05/06/07 above, for the same reason --
# predictions/ (33MB, 575 files) and scores/ (117MB, 575 files: one per (isoform,
# combo, repeat, fold), including the CYP2D6 extended-pool addendum's combos) are
# bulk per-fold raw output, individually small but not worth tracking -- checked
# directly, not assumed. Both are fully regeneratable by
# re-running the notebook (deterministic: reuses 05's own manifest.csv seeds for
# bootstrap scoring, and simple-averages already-frozen 05/06/07 predictions -- no
# retraining, so no separate `--retrain` script exists here). combo_summary_table.csv,
# pairwise_comparisons.csv, step3_summary.csv, and figures/ stay tracked -- all are
# small and are what the notebook reports from / step 4 consumes directly.
outputs/08_ensemble_selection/predictions/
outputs/08_ensemble_selection/scores/

# 10_final_retrain_predict (final full-dataset retrain + blind-test predict,
# scripts/10_final_retrain_predict.py): chemprop_runs/ (~500MB, checked directly --
# 2 configs' worth of Chemprop checkpoints/logs, larger per-run than 05/06 since this
# trains on the full ~4,900-compound pool rather than a ~3,900-compound CV fold) is
# excluded, same reasoning as 05/06 above -- fully regeneratable by re-running the
# script (deterministic: fixed SEED=42 throughout, and the resumability check skips
# any config whose blind_predictions/ output already exists). blind_predictions/
# (6 small CSVs, ~350KB total -- the actual task deliverable) and config_manifest.csv
# stay tracked.
outputs/10_final_retrain_predict/chemprop_runs/

# 11b_caruana_selection (Caruana bagged ensemble selection + size-cap revision,
# notebook-only -- no companion script): predictions/ (2.0MB, 100 files) and scores/
# (14MB, 100 files) are the per-(repeat, fold) weighted-ensemble outputs from
# `score_weighted_ensemble_per_fold` -- bulk raw output, individually small but not
# worth tracking, checked directly not assumed -- same treatment as 05/06/07/08 above.
# Fully regeneratable by re-running the notebook (deterministic: reuses 05's own
# manifest.csv bootstrap seeds; no retraining, just reweighting already-frozen
# 11_caruana_prep OOF predictions). weights.csv/weights_uncapped.csv, summary.csv,
# cap_comparison.csv, marginal_value_trajectory.csv,
# placement_correction_diagnostic.csv, recalibration_params.csv, and figures/ all
# stay tracked -- small, and what this notebook (and notebook 12) actually read/
# report from.
outputs/11b_caruana_selection/predictions/
outputs/11b_caruana_selection/scores/

# 12_caruana_retrain_predict (Caruana-weighted full retrain + blind predict,
# scripts/12_caruana_retrain_predict.py): chemprop_runs/ (9MB, checked directly --
# the one chemprop_randominit full-data training run this step needed; everything
# else was reused from notebook 10's own chemprop_runs/ above) is excluded, same
# reasoning as 10_final_retrain_predict above -- fully regeneratable by re-running
# the script (deterministic: fixed SEED=42, resumability skip logic).
# tabular_mordred_pca_blind_test.csv (1.9MB) is also excluded -- a deterministic
# `.transform()`-only feature artifact (the already-fitted train-only pipeline
# applied to the blind test set), mirroring how its train-side counterpart
# (`data/processed/tabular_mordred_pca.csv`) is already covered by the blanket
# `data/processed/` exclusion above; regeneratable by re-running the script's
# mordred-transform stage. blind_predictions/ (784KB -- the actual per-config
# deliverable), config_provenance.csv, and both submission_candidate*.csv files
# stay tracked.
outputs/12_caruana_retrain_predict/chemprop_runs/
outputs/12_caruana_retrain_predict/tabular_mordred_pca_blind_test.csv
